details.image_prompt:
{
  "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition features two plates, one sharp in the foreground and one slightly blurred in the background, set on a rustic aged oak table. Camera angle is a 3/4 overhead view, capturing the full arrangement. The scene is bathed in soft, natural light from a window on the left, creating gentle shadows. Each plate holds two whole-wheat waffles toasted to a golden-brown, crisp texture. A generous dollop of smooth, thick white Skyr, swirled with vanilla and cinnamon, is dolloped artfully over the waffles, with a warm, dark purple blueberry compote spooned on top, showing softened, burst berries and syrupy juices dripping down the sides. The dish is topped with a rustic scattering of nutty hemp hearts and coarse, earthy chopped walnuts. Props include a small, rumpled linen napkin tucked under one plate and a small wooden spoon resting casually on the wood surface near a few stray fallen blueberries and walnut crumbs. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating — lived-in, warm, authentic. Slight natural imperfections: asymmetric garnish placement, a small sauce drip on the plate rim, slightly uneven browning on the waffles. Include subtle traces of the cooking process: a few stray hemp hearts on the table. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from professional cookbook photography."
}
